# Normalise line endings across platforms.
#
# Without this, Windows clones with core.autocrlf=true get CRLF while CI
# (Linux) checks out LF. Prettier's default endOfLine is "lf", so the same file
# fails `pnpm run check` locally and passes in CI — local runs report ~78 files
# while CI reports 16, which makes the check untrustworthy on Windows.
#
# Text files are stored as LF in the repository and checked out as LF
# everywhere. Binary assets are left untouched.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary file types: never attempt EOL conversion or diff-as-text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary

# Large generated datasets that may appear in git-mode deployments.
*.fit binary
*.tcx binary
*.gpx binary
